N:canyonos
D:Deploy, observe, and scale multi-agent Python applications without decorators or SDK modifications using CanyonOS (v0.2.2). Use when converting plain Python, LangChain, or LangGraph projects into containerized agent replicas via .canyon and prepare.py; defining workflow topologies, entrypoints, and adapters; configuring state isolation, replicas, and autoscaling in scaling.yaml; managing LLM access and cost caps in llms.yaml; extracting versioned system prompts into prompts.yaml; generating OpenTelemetry metrics and traces; or running canyonos doctor, new-app, validate, deploy, status, test, logs, clean, and stop. Route Kubernetes-only CRD declarative cluster controllers to kagent, MCP application authoring to fastmcp, and LLM evaluation benchmarks to trulens or agent-evaluation.
G:canyonos multi-agent orchestration agent-deployment scaling observability containerization opentelemetry python
U[5]:
  Convert existing Python or LangChain multi-agent projects into CanyonOS container topologies
  Configure agent state boundaries, replicas, and autoscaling policies in scaling.yaml
  Govern model access, budget limits, and token rate caps across agents in llms.yaml
  Extract and version hardcoded system prompts in prompts.yaml without modifying source code
  Validate and deploy multi-agent services with OpenTelemetry tracing and GPU metrics
S[6]{n,action,details}:
  1,Preflight,Run scripts/preflight.py --json to verify tool binaries and pinned source manifest offline
  2,Convert,Execute prepare.py to generate isolated .canyon configuration and agent adapters
  3,Topology,Define workflow endpoint, agent functions, and replica parameters in workflow_config.yaml
  4,Policies,Establish autoscaling rules in scaling.yaml, LLM budgets in llms.yaml, and prompts.yaml
  5,Validate,Run canyonos validate to statically check imports, entrypoints, and uv lockfile dependencies
  6,Deploy&Test,Deploy with canyonos deploy --serve false and dispatch verification queries with canyonos test
R[5]:
  Run scripts/preflight.py --json before executing container commands or provisioning infrastructure
  Never copy or commit dotenv files into .canyon; keep secrets strictly in project root for container runtime
  Static pre-deployment validation via canyonos validate must exit 0 before requesting deployment approval
  Isolate in-process stateful agents to single replicas (replicas: 1) to prevent distributed state divergence
  Route raw Kubernetes CRD controllers to kagent and generic MCP server authoring to fastmcp
